  "step_3": "The decision reason depends on the presence of a sure (100% certain) outcome in either lottery, which is not the case in this problem—both lotteries involve risk and no sure payoffs. Therefore, the reason cannot meaningfully apply. Moreover, the individual's verbal report focuses on the higher potential gain and perceived expected value, not on certainty or guaranteed outcomes. There is no indication that the individual considered whether one option was certain or preferred an option due to certainty. The reasoning in the report is based on outcome magnitude and probability comparison, not on the presence of a sure outcome. Thus, both the applicability of the reason and the content of the report suggest the reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
